      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1d2d8912011a98b15beddf365150d2b6cb248dba43efcb993406adfeb0f91f71",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Two cutoff factorizations of zeta preserve different claims. The shortened approximate-functional-equation polynomial is represented by smooth and rough Dirichlet-polynomial factors only in a quantified mean-square sense. The smoothed Euler-Hadamard construction instead separates prime and zero contributions in a hybrid product; changing its cutoff alters the individual factors, while the theorem and the reported local plots concern compensation in their product.",
