    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1fd4877c474e78921276ef0673e626a7cfb66a7e09b722b9ec8351b992d32606",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The full-moment program conjecturally separates a zeta leading constant into a prime arithmetic factor and a density-calibrated unitary factor, with the latter computed exactly only in the matrix ensemble. For truncated objects there is a stronger bridge: the zeta pseudomoment has a proved leading factor a_k vol(P_k), while a truncated unitary characteristic-polynomial moment equals a lattice count whose normalized limit is the same substochastic-polytope volume.",
