      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_62a3a641e76f8fa17247721415832464abea2d6235d1fb46234e4009f7110e23",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "High-moment tail bounds have an analytic capacity constraint: the moment order can amplify a deviation only while the resulting Dirichlet polynomial fits the averaging interval. Optimizing within that constraint yields source-specific quadratic and V log V upper-tail regimes. In a multiscale maximum proof, the same optimization is applied after a union over locations and prime blocks, so the barrier includes padding that pays the grid entropy.",
