    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a9c6efb2f9597c8e6e1d1617500cefbe575fa746cd15a50e333b19d50f983697",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At second-moment level, an Atkinson-type intermediate formula and full-versus-truncated Voronoi representations organize generalized-divisor oscillations under explicit convergence and cutoff controls. In higher critical-line moment programs, expanding powers of zeta instead creates shifted divisor correlations; with long polynomials, distinct rational-direction strata can contribute proposed main terms and must be retained separately.",
