    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c95621584f30af3f8d05f5b5acfa364be730961a538a563e4408aab737d25f9e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The GCD-resonance construction separates arithmetic design from analytic transfer. A multiplicative support is optimized and compressed according to logarithmic ratios, the frequencies visible after integrating against the resonator. A separate positive-series lemma and compact-frequency convolution then retain a favorable block of approximate relations km near n and convert it, under localization and length budgets, into an existence lower bound for a zeta extreme.",
