    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_da5a9938386ae9b5f9e180d7144918a83da303a37ab91451f16411d8df357c87",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both analyses delay a boundary operation until an auxiliary analytic representation has been constructed and matched on an overlap. In the ladder-height analysis, a contour integral continues the original germ and boundary derivatives recover zeta-valued Taylor coefficients. In the mean-square analysis, a two-variable identity is continued before the variables are coupled, specialized, and integrated. A separate finite cutoff is still needed when a boundedly convergent Voronoi series is inserted into an improper integral.",
